<title>USA: Rhone Rorer gets OK for Tilade for kids.</title>
<headline>Rhone Rorer gets OK for Tilade for kids.</headline>
<dateline>COLLEGEVILLE, Pa. 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc said Monday that it has received clearance from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to extend the therapeutic benefits of Tilade Inhaler to children ages six to eleven.</p>
<p>Tilade, an inhaled anti-inflammatory drug indicated as maintenance therapy in the management of patients with mild-to-moderate bronchial asthma, was previously indicated for patients 12 and older.</p>
